.TH STOP-MU2EDAQ-NOTIFY-PROXY.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-phone-notification-system 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
stop-mu2edaq-notify-proxy.sh \- stop the reverse tunnel, optionally also the local server and EC2 Caddy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scripts/stop\-mu2edaq\-notify\-proxy.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stops the pid\-file reverse tunnel (SIGTERM, up to 5 s, then SIGKILL) and
removes the pid file. By default it leaves the local server, remote Caddy and
the EC2 instance running. It does not touch the
.B org.mu2edaq.notify-proxy-tunnel
launchd agent: a tunnel run by that agent has no pid file here and keeps
running, so the public edge stays up. Boot the agent out with
.B launchctl bootout
(as
.BR stop-mu2edaq-notify-chain.sh (1)
does) to drop it.
.SH OPTIONS
None; everything is set by environment variables.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I data/mu2edaq-notify-proxy-tunnel.pid
Tunnel pid file.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_STOP_SERVER
1 also runs
.BR stop-mu2edaq-notify-server.sh (1).
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_STOP_REMOTE_CADDY
1 also runs
.B sudo systemctl stop caddy
on the instance.
.TP
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_USER ", " MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_KEY ", " MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PROXY_PIDFILE
As for
.BR start-mu2edaq-notify-proxy.sh (1).
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0, unless
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_STOP_REMOTE_CADDY=1
and the key is missing, the instance has no address, or the remote stop fails.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
scripts/stop\-mu2edaq\-notify\-proxy.sh
MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_STOP_REMOTE_CADDY=1 scripts/stop\-mu2edaq\-notify\-proxy.sh
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start-mu2edaq-notify-proxy.sh (1),
.BR stop-mu2edaq-notify-chain.sh (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ Group. Part of
.BR mu2edaq-phone-notification-system .
